# License overview

Keybow Firmware Plus is a fork of [Pimoroni's Keybow firmware](https://github.com/pimoroni/keybow-firmware). This repository contains components under different licenses; there is no single license covering every file.

| Component | License / attribution |
| --- | --- |
| Original Keybow C firmware, Lua scripts, and example patterns | MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Pimoroni Ltd. The original MIT grant is reproduced below. |
| Keybow Firmware Plus editor code and project-created assets | MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 ThoughtfulDev; see [`editor/LICENSE`](editor/LICENSE). |
| bcm2835 1.68 | GPL-3.0-only; full text in [`bcm2835-1.68/COPYING`](bcm2835-1.68/COPYING). |
| libusbgx | LGPL-2.1-or-later library; GPL-2.0-or-later example sources. See [`libusbgx/COPYING.LGPL`](libusbgx/COPYING.LGPL) and [`libusbgx/COPYING`](libusbgx/COPYING). |
| Lua 5.4.0 | MIT; copyright notice and license are in [`lua-5.4.0/doc/readme.html`](lua-5.4.0/doc/readme.html). |
| Raspberry Pi boot firmware | Broadcom/Raspberry Pi binary redistribution terms in [`sdcard/LICENCE.broadcom`](sdcard/LICENCE.broadcom). |
| Linux kernel and initrd packages | Kernel is GPL-2.0; initrd packages retain their individual notices under `/usr/share/doc/*/copyright`. See [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for firmware provenance and source-availability status. |
| Desktop app dependencies | Individual licenses and required notices are summarized in [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md); package builds include that file. |

The `keybow` executable statically links bundled components, including bcm2835 and libusbgx. Its distribution is therefore subject to the applicable copyleft terms as well as the source-code obligations described in the component licenses. Do not treat the original MIT grant as applying to the combined executable or the entire repository.

